                        "review": "NAL Is Alive is one of those games where you start thinking: “I’ll just check it out for a bit.”\n\nAnd then, somehow, an hour later you’re still there, fully locked in, actually caring about what’s happening on the screen 😅\n\nIt doesn’t feel like you’re just playing a game. It feels more like you’ve been pulled into its world a little. And every now and then it throws something at you that makes you go: “okay… I did NOT expect that.”\n\nThe gameplay isn’t about being overly complicated for no reason. It’s more about keeping you slightly on edge, never letting you fully relax — and it does that really well.\n\nAnd the worst part (in a good way) is that you keep wanting to stop… but there’s always that thought: “okay, just five more minutes…” 👀\n\nNAL Is Alive isn’t the kind of game you just finish and forget.\nIt’s the kind that quietly stays in your head long after you’ve closed it 😄",
